{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,14.011,1.643,1.471,"US Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"22 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,7.46,3.651,3.268,"Uber"],[13.889,14.731,31.145,2.373,2.124,"Priced as if margins have peaked"],[13.889,20.845,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Uber closed at $63.47 on 20 November, a 52-week low, 31% below its"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"December 2025 high of $92.57 (YTD −22%) and 9% below where it closed on"],[13.889,23.733,52.931,1.809,1.634,"the day of a Q3 beat. It trades on 14.4x FY27E consensus EPS of $4.41 and an"],[13.889,25.177,52.931,1.809,1.634,"8.1% FY26E free-cash-flow yield. The fear is robotaxis: Waymo and Tesla"],[13.889,26.621,52.931,1.809,1.634,"running fleets that bypass Uber’s network. At our 10.0% WACC the price"],[13.889,28.065,52.931,1.809,1.634,"discounts EQe FY27E free cash flow growing 2.5% a year forever; with the"],[13.889,29.509,52.934,1.809,1.634,"operating margin frozen at this year’s 3.8% of bookings, our DCF still gives"],[13.889,30.954,34.293,1.809,1.634,"$72. We rate UBER Overweight, Dec-27 target $95."],[13.889,33.439,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Q3 Non-GAAP EPS rose 35% to $0.88. Gross bookings grew 20% to $59.8bn"],[13.889,34.883,52.987,1.809,1.634,"and Non-GAAP operating income 38%, a margin of 3.85% of bookings from"],[13.889,36.328,52.934,1.809,1.634,"3.37%. Revenue grew only 10% because business-model changes cut 8 points"],[13.889,37.772,52.964,1.809,1.634,"(Mobility revenue −2%), so we forecast on bookings. Mobility earned 8.0% of"],[13.889,39.216,52.931,1.809,1.634,"its bookings, Delivery 3.7%. Q1–Q3 EPS landed on average 92% of the way up"],[13.889,40.684,52.931,1.809,1.634,"the guided range; on the same basis Q4 is $0.99. With bookings +17% and the"],[13.889,42.128,52.931,1.809,1.634,"margin +35bp a year, EQe FY27E EPS is $4.23, 4% below consensus, and"],[13.889,43.572,47.253,1.809,1.634,"FY28E $5.36. GAAP EPS ($0.25 in Q3) swings with stake revaluations."],[13.889,46.034,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Our $95 target averages 14.7x FY28E EPS (six-peer median) plus equity stakes"],[13.889,47.502,52.962,1.809,1.634,"at 80% of book ($5 a share), $84, and a ten-year DCF of Non-GAAP operating"],[13.889,48.946,52.936,1.809,1.634,"income less legal and restructuring costs (rf 4.92%, beta 1.33, margin capped at"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"5.5% of bookings, terminal growth 2.5%), $103. Uber has offered €41.50 a"],[13.889,51.834,52.931,1.809,1.634,"share for Delivery Hero ($14.8bn equity, closing H2 2027, funded with cash and"],[13.889,53.278,52.936,1.809,1.634,"debt); it is not in our forecasts beyond the 24.99% stake already held. What"],[13.889,54.722,52.992,1.809,1.634,"would prove us wrong: robotaxis taking share or price, visible as Mobility"],[13.889,56.167,52.931,1.809,1.634,"bookings growth below 10% or its margin falling; an AV bear case (growth to"],[13.889,57.611,52.951,1.809,1.634,"zero by FY32, margin frozen) is worth $43. The street mean is $98 (46 analysts)."],[13.889,60.098,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.758,68.709,0.999,1.022,0.915,"60"],[15.758,66.942,0.999,1.022,0.915,"70"],[15.758,65.174,0.999,1.022,0.915,"80"],[15.758,63.407,0.999,1.022,0.915,"90"],[15.268,61.639,1.489,1.022,0.915,"100"],[17.8,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.424,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.293,69.404,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[31.901,69.404,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.929,70.575,3.857,1.275,1.111,"UBER ($)"],[25.566,70.575,7.626,1.275,1.111,"S&P 500 (rebased)"],[20.481,71.735,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.166,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.081,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,71.735,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,72.8,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[18.98,72.8,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−22.3%"],[23.664,72.8,2.842,1.387,1.209,"−7.9%"],[28.028,72.8,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−19.2%"],[32.945,72.8,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−23.9%"],[15.492,73.866,1.4